ma D t) and log-divergent burst sums: genuinely critical, slow i.o. bursts not excluded. Labeled illustration (Gamma=2, H=8, m_c=6, 30000 steps): m=3,4,5 grow throughout; m=6: F = 830 ~ sqrt(24 t) (the sqrt-critical signature; expected bursts by this horizon ~0.5, observed 0); m=7,8: F = 30119/60056 (linear), zero bursts. Gamma=3, H=2 (m_c=5): m=3,4 grow; m=5 log-slow sporadic growth then quiet; m=6: growth freezes a.s. (the process does not halt; bursts stop).",
